  "question": {
    "text": "During the reaction of permanganate with thiosulphate, the change in oxidation of manganese occurs by value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>. Identify which of the below medium will favour the reaction.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6MzIR",
      "text": "Both aqueous acidic and neutral",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JxWRV",
      "text": "Aqueous neutral",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xLcrC",
      "text": "Both aqueous acidic and faintly alkaline",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hct0g",
      "text": "Aqueous acidic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In neutral or weakly alkaline solution oxidation state of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math>&nbsp;changes by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;unit.&nbsp;The reaction between permanganate and thiosulfate is a redox reaction, in which permanganate acts as an oxidizing agent and thiosulfate acts as a reducing agent.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#8861;</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>This ionic mechanism is favoured in neutral aqueous medium.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
